# File spec for ./vyniltest.rs — the `Test` document schema plus the single-Test
# assert-evaluation engine. Loading, merged templating, mock injection, install execution,
# timing and the Err posture live in ./handler.rs (./handler.sdd pending): referenced
# here as collaborator truth, never restated.

Spec: VynilTest

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Hold the serde shape of the `Test` document — @VynilTest, @VynilTestMeta,
    @VynilTestInstance, @VynilTestSetRef, deserialized by ./handler.rs — and provide the
    complete assert engine @VynilTest::run_asserts: selector matching, JSON-subset value
    comparison, the six matcher verdicts in a value-bearing and a bare lane, and every
    verbatim pass/fail message string, over a borrowed snapshot of mock-created
    @Dynamic objects. Also exposes @appslug, the `instance.appslug` slug builder used by
    the handler's templating context. Total by design: a failing assert is a
    @VynilAssertResult row, never an error and never a panic; this file performs no I/O,
    no Handlebars, no Rhai, no cluster access and no clock reads.

Owns:
  ./vyniltest.rs

References:
  ./vyniltestset.sdd — the shared assert vocabulary this engine consumes (@VynilAssert,
    @VynilAssertMatch, @VynilAssertSelector, @VynilAssertResult, @VynilTestSetMocks); its
    wire shapes are not restated here.
  ./handler.rs — consumer, sole caller (./handler.sdd pending): loads `Test` documents via
    @serde_json::from_value after the scanner's apiVersion/kind gate (duplicate-name
    abort), pre-templates every selector/value/mock and merges @testSets before any
    evaluation happens here, and runs the whole suite flow around @run_asserts:
    @./handler.rs @TestHandler::get_templated_test builds the Handlebars context with
    @appslug as `instance.appslug`, resolves per-reference variables in precedence
    reference-override first, then testSet @default, then JSON null, and adds undeclared
    reference-only names (@build_var_context — the variable precedence the `Test`
    schema merely carries, resolved entirely outside this file); @Script::new_mock injects
    the kubernetes/http mocks; the install lane is one Rhai @eval (context then install);
    there is no wait/settle posture anywhere — asserts evaluate once over the
    created-objects snapshot.
  ./handler.rs — truth on the two postures the `Test` types feed: Err-vs-failed-assert is
    decided in @TestHandler::run_test, which folds any @common::Error into one synthetic
    `execution` failed @VynilAssertResult row and times each test with
    @std::time::Instant around @run_test_inner, so @run_asserts itself has no error lane
    and no duration; and the validate_refs referenced by ./../package/test.sdd is
    @TestHandler::validate_refs in ./handler.rs — it reads @VynilTestSetRef.testSet
    declared here, and is never called from ./../package/test.rs (open there as its own
    task).
  ./../package/test.sdd — CLI driver; its run/summary/@Error::TestFailure lane sits two
    calls above @run_asserts.
  ./result.sdd — consumer of the produced rows: they are appended by ./handler.rs and
    rendered there into text/json/JUnit; the shape here is their only production site
    besides the synthetic rows in ./handler.rs.
  ./mod.rs — module re-export of @VynilTest alone; @appslug, @VynilTestMeta,
    @VynilTestInstance and @VynilTestSetRef reach other ./handler.rs code through the
    `vyniltest::` path (crate surface `client::testing::vyniltest::*` via
    /agent/src/lib.rs `pub mod testing`).
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Dynamic, the object representation selected, labeled,
    serialized and compared here; the selection snapshot itself is produced upstream by
    the mock k8s layer of `vynil-core` (objects land in the shared created vec only
    through mock apply calls, which merge the matching mock input — a bare `mocks` entry
    never reaches @run_asserts unless a script re-applies it).

Depends on:
  ./vyniltestset.rs types — the five imported items; matcher wire forms (`all`, `any`,
    `none`, `exact: N`, `at_least: N`, `at_most: N`, N @u64) are frozen there.
  `serde`/`serde_json` — the derives, and the @serde_json::Value round-trip every value
    comparison rides.

Exposes:
  @appslug — `#[must_use] pub fn(@pkg: &@str, @inst: &@str) -> @String`: when @pkg equals
    @inst returns @inst untouched (no length clamp); otherwise `{inst}-{pkg}` truncated to
    the first `28` Unicode scalar chars (@chars().take, not bytes, no word-boundary care);
    no lowercasing, no charset sanitization. ./handler.rs injects the result as
    `instance.appslug` in the templating context.
  @VynilTest — `#[allow(non_snake_case)]` root with @Deserialize/@Serialize/@Clone/@Debug:
    @apiVersion (@String), @kind (@String), @metadata (@VynilTestMeta), @instance
    (@VynilTestInstance, not @Option), @testSets (@Option<Vec<@VynilTestSetRef>>), @mocks
    (@Option<@VynilTestSetMocks> — the shared envelope owned by ./vyniltestset.sdd),
    @asserts (@Option<Vec<@VynilAssert>>).
  @VynilTestMeta — @name (@String), @description (@Option<@String>).
  @VynilTestInstance — @name (@String), @namespace (@String, both required), @options
    (@Option<@BTreeMap<@String, @serde_json::Value>>).
  @VynilTestSetRef — `#[allow(non_snake_case)]` @testSet (@String), @variables
    (@Option<@BTreeMap<@String, @serde_json::Value>> — name → raw value, typed unlike the
    TestSet variable declarations).
  @VynilTest::run_asserts — `#[must_use]` engine entry: `(&self, generated: &[Dynamic]) -> Vec<VynilAssertResult>`;
    the whole observable engine behaviour below.
  Internal helpers are private but their effects are user-visible in @message strings and
    are therefore fully specified here: @json_subset_match, @json_subset_diff,
    @object_label, @matches_selector, @no_match_hint, @detail_lines, @value_verdict,
    @count_verdict.

Accepts:
  A `Test` document mapping produced by the ./handler.rs scanner (gate
    `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1`, kind `Test`, duplicate-name abort — none re-validated
    here). Required wire keys: `apiVersion`, `kind`, `metadata` with `name`, and
    `instance` with both `name` and `namespace`; optional: `description`, `testSets`,
    `mocks`, `asserts`, `instance.options`. No container rename and no
    `deny_unknown_fields`, so keys are exactly the field spellings (camelCase
    `apiVersion`/`testSets` survive via `#[allow(non_snake_case)]`) and unknown keys are
    dropped; no `#[serde(default)]` — optionality is @Option-only, absent and `null`
    alike. @apiVersion/@kind carry no constraint: the templated clone from
    ./handler.rs keeps whatever strings arrived, and @run_asserts reads neither.
  @run_asserts accepts any borrowed @Dynamic slice: the object pool handed over by
    ./handler.rs after the install script ran (created/merged snapshot, see References);
    elements that are not rhai maps are invisible to selection and to hints alike.

Returns:
  @run_asserts: one @VynilAssertResult per assert, in assert order, always the same
    length as @self.asserts (@Option::None and `Some(vec![])` both yield an empty vec —
    the caller re-collapses empty to @None anyway); @name/@description are cloned from the
    assert, @passed/@message from the verdict lane chosen below.
  @appslug: the slug string per the two branches above.

Raises:
  Nothing — no @Result anywhere in this file. Every fallible read is guarded:
    @Dynamic::as_map_ref via @let-else, enum-string reads via @and_then/@unwrap_or_default,
    counts via @usize::try_from(...).unwrap_or(@usize::MAX) (lossy only on 32-bit
    targets: oversized counts saturate, making `exact`/`at_least` unsatisfiable and
    `at_most` always-true), and all indexings in @run_asserts/@detail_lines use @Vec::get +
    @Option::map_or_else. There is no bare @unwrap()/@expect() and therefore no panic
    site; the only data loss is the silent JSON round-trip collapse noted in Handles.

Handles:
  Zero-selection fast path — when a selector matches nothing and the matcher is not
    `none`/`at_most(_)` (any `N`), the row is produced without touching @value:
    @passed false, @message set to @no_match_hint over the full pool —
    `no objects matched selector`, or the longer
    `no objects matched selector (did you mean: {labels})` — `{labels}` the
    comma-joined labels — for every pool object whose
    `kind` or `metadata.name` equals a selector
    field case-insensitively while the exact comparison rejected them (@eq_ignore_ascii_case
    on those two fields only — `namespace` never seeds a hint; either single field is
    enough, so a same-named `Service` is suggested for a missing `StatefulSet`/web);
    `none` and `at_most(_)` fall through and pass vacuously at count `0`.
  JSON round-trip collapse — @run_asserts serializes each selected @Dynamic to a string
    and reparses; any per-object failure (@serde_json::to_string -> `""` ->
    @serde_json::from_str fail) silently degrades that one object to a JSON `null` for
    value comparison (labels still read the live @Dynamic), and a comparison against
    null is just a normal diff against `null`, never an abort.

Must:
  # ── Engine flow, fixed order, per assert, asserts kept in document order ──
  Select: @selected = elements of @generated where @matches_selector is true, input order
    preserved; @total = @selected.len().
  If @total == `0` and the matcher is neither @VynilAssertMatch::@None nor
    @VynilAssertMatch::@AtMost(_), emit the fail/hint row (Handles) and skip value work
    even when @value is present — a zero hit never shows expected-vs-actual diffs.
  Otherwise branch on @value: @None → @count_verdict(matcher, total); @Some → map each
    selected object through the JSON round-trip, partition index ranges
    `(0..total)` on @json_subset_match(value, json) (matched / non-matched index
    vectors, both order-preserving), then @value_verdict(matcher, matching, total) with
    two lazily-evaluated detail closures: non-matched indices with JSON diffs, matched
    indices with `(matched)` labels.
  Copy @name/@description verbatim into the row; never reorder, merge, drop or re-title
    results relative to the assert list.
  # ── @matches_selector: exact, case-sensitive, field-by-field ──
  A non-map object matches every selector. If @kind is @Some, the object's top-level
    `kind` must deserialize as a string exactly equal to it (missing or non-string kind
    fails a kind selector); the comparison is case-sensitive — only the hint scan
    lowercases.
  With @name and @namespace both @None the object matches right after the kind check —
    an `object without any metadata field` passes a kind-only selector.
  Otherwise `metadata` must exist and be a map. @Some(name)/@Some(namespace) each demand
    an exactly equal string at @metadata.name/@metadata.namespace: absent or non-string
    metadata fields match nothing, and an explicit empty-string selector is a literal
    ask for an empty value, NOT a wildcard — only a @None (omitted or `null` key) selects
    all.
  # ── @json_subset_match: expected ⊆ actual ──
  Object ⊆ object when every expected key exists in actual and recurses; arrays match
    when every expected element has at least one actual element matching it — unordered
    and by existence, so duplicates and extra actual members are ignored; every other
    pairing is plain @serde_json::Value equality, hence scalar compare is
    type-strict (`1` does not equal `1.0`, `true` not `1`), null and missing-key are
    distinct, and `k: null` in expected requires an actual `k: null`.
  # ── value lane @value_verdict: `matching` of `total`, messages verbatim ──
  `all`: pass iff `matching == total` → `{matching}/{total} match`; fail →
    `{matching}/{total} match, expected all` + non-matched diff detail.
  `any`: pass iff `matching > 0` → `{matching}/{total} match`; fail →
    `0/{total} match, expected at least one` + non-matched diff detail.
  `exact N`: pass iff `matching == N` AND ALSO `total == N` (a bigger selection failing
    nothing extra still fails) → `{matching}/{total} match`; fail →
    `{matching}/{total} match, expected exactly {N}` + non-matched diff detail; a
    32-bit-saturated N (`usize::MAX`) can never pass.
  `at_least N`: pass iff `matching >= N` → `{matching}/{total} match`; fail →
    `{matching}/{total} match, expected at least {N}` + non-matched diff detail.
  `at_most N`: pass iff `matching <= N` → `{matching}/{total} match`; fail →
    `{matching}/{total} match, expected at most {N}` + matched `(matched)` detail — the
    fail detail lists the offending MATCHES, unlike all/any/exact/at_least which list
    the misses.
  `none`: pass iff `matching == 0` → `0/{total} match as expected`; fail →
    `{matching}/{total} match, expected none` + matched `(matched)` detail.
  # ── count lane @count_verdict: bare matcher on total; never appends detail ──
  Bare `all` runs the same arm as bare `any`: pass iff `total > 0` → `{total} match`,
    fail only at `0` → `0 match, expected at least one`.
  `exact N`: pass iff `total == N` → `{total} match`; fail →
    `{total} match, expected exactly {N}`.
  `at_least N`: pass iff `total >= N` → `{total} match`; fail →
    `{total} match, expected at least {N}`.
  `at_most N`: pass iff `total <= N` → `{total} match`; fail →
    `{total} match, expected at most {N}` (true also at `total == 0`).
  `none`: pass iff total `0` → `0 match as expected`; fail → `{total} match, expected none`.
  # ── detail rendering (the only multi-line message sources) ──
  @object_label: rhai map's `kind` and @metadata.name/@namespace with missing/non-string
    parts defaulting to empty → `{kind}/{name}` when the namespace reads empty else
    `{kind}/{ns}/{name}`; a non-map object labels `<unknown>`.
  @detail_lines: empty index list → @String::new, so a fail phrase can stand alone; else
    the message grows a leading newline (`\n`) and one two-space-indented line per index:
    `  {label}` bare when the diff pass finds nothing (defensive — a listed non-match
    normally yields ≥ 1 diff), `  {label} (matched)` in the label pass, `  {label}: ` +
    comma-joined diffs in the diff pass.
  @json_subset_diff walks expected only: dot-path from the root object at `.key` (`.a.b`
    nested), array misses as `{path}[{i}]: no match found for {expected-element}` with `i`
    counting EXPECTED positions (root array prints `[0]`, under a key `.a[0]`), a present
    key printing recursively, a missing key as `{path}: expected {v}, got <missing>`, and
    any leaf mismatch or scalar/type divergence as
    `{path}: expected {expected}, got {actual}` — a root-level scalar value has an empty
    path, so its line starts with `: `.
    Actual-only keys are never reported.
  Keep @appslug exact-branch: the `pkg == inst` shortcut bypasses the 28-char budget;
    truncation applies only to the `{inst}-{pkg}` composite, counted in chars so one
    multi-byte scalar costs one slot.

Must not:
  Return an error, panic, or mutate @self — abort posture, @Err-to-`execution`-row
    folding and @Duration timing belong to @TestHandler::run_test (./handler.rs), and a
    failed assert must stay a data row.
  Render Handlebars or run Rhai: selectors, values and messages the asserts carry arrive
    already templated from ./handler.rs; the only interpolation here is the engine's own
    Rust format strings above.
  Resolve @testSets, @variables or precedence of any kind — @VynilTestSetRef is opaque
    cargo merged upstream (@build_var_context per References); likewise no
    reference-existence check (@TestHandler::validate_refs stays in ./handler.rs,
    uncalled).
  Re-run, retry or wait: one pass over the snapshot handed by the caller, no settle loop.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the scenarios below to same-named tests — this file has no #[cfg(test)] module
      and nothing in-tree calls @run_asserts: selector-kind-only-no-metadata,
      selector-empty-string-literal, zero-hit-hint-did-you-mean,
      zero-hit-none-and-at-most-vacuous-pass, count-lane-bare-matchers-including-all-eq-any,
      subset-match-arrays-unordered-and-strict-numbers,
      exact-value-lane-requires-total-eq-n, fail-detail-shapes-diffs-vs-matched-labels,
      serialization-collapse-to-null, appslug-equals-bare-vs-28-char-composite.
  [?] Bare `all` (no value) is an alias of `any` — existence, not universality — and its
      fail line even says `expected at least one`. Decide whether that is the intended
      reading or `all` should be invalid without a value.
  [?] Value-lane `exact N` additionally requires `total == N`, so 2-of-3 objects matching
      fails although 2 matched; count-lane `exact` checks only `total`. Decide whether the
      value-lane second condition is intended or matching == N suffices.
  [?] @appslug: unexplained 28-char budget and the `pkg == inst` branch skips it, so a
      long package-equal name escapes truncation. Decide the real budget (DNS label?) and
      whether the shortcut must clamp too.
  [ ] Findings to review, left untouched by this documentary pass: the zero-hit hint
      hides every expected-vs-actual diff behind `no objects matched selector` even for
      value-bearing asserts; the hint scans only kind/name case-insensitively, never
      namespace; and a broken object collapses silently to `null` instead of surfacing
      the serialization failure. Decide whether to keep or revisit each.

Done when:
  Each scenario has a passing same-named test, the `[?]` records above are answered, and
    `cargo test -p agent`, clippy, `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: no asserts evaluates to nothing
  Given @VynilTest with @asserts @Option::None or `Some` of an empty vec
  When @run_asserts over any pool
  Then the result vec is empty in both cases

Scenario: kind-only selector and the metadata short-circuit
  Given pool object `Deployment` (a map) with NO metadata field at all
  When selector is kind-only (`kind: Deployment`, name/namespace absent)
  Then the object is selected — the check returns before touching metadata
  But Given selector kind `deployment` lowercase
  Then it selects nothing (matching is case-sensitive; only hints lowercase)

Scenario: empty-string selectors are literals not wildcards
  Given selector `name: ""` against an object with metadata.name `web` or with no name key
  Then neither matches — an empty value is demanded exactly; wildcard needs the key absent

Scenario: zero-hit hint keeps the value to itself
  Given assert `matcher: exact: 2`, `value: {spec: {replicas: 3}}`, selector kind `StatefulSet` name `web`,
    pool holding only `Service/prod/web`
  Then @passed false and message `no objects matched selector (did you mean: Service/prod/web)`
    — name-only case-insensitive hit suggests it; the `{spec}` expectation is never diffed;
    pool order survives into the hint list

Scenario: zero-hit vacuous pass for none and at_most
  Given selector matching nothing, `matcher: none`
  When @run_asserts runs
  Then @passed true with value `None` → message `0 match as expected`,
    and value Some → `0/0 match as expected`
  And Given `at_most: 0` at zero hits → passed (`0 match` / `0/0 match`), while `all`,
    `any`, `at_least`, `exact` take the hint fail path instead

Scenario: value-lane subset comparison is structural
  Given two selected objects, expected `{metadata: {labels: {app: a}}}`
  When actual objects carry extra keys and one array in actual contains the expected
    element among others
  Then `all` passes with `2/2 match` — extra actual members are free; expected `1` against
    actual `1.0` fails (strict scalar); unordered array membership passes by existence.

Scenario: exact needs the whole selection to be the payload
  Given three selected objects of which two satisfy @value, `matcher: exact: 2`
  Then @passed false, message starts `2/3 match, expected exactly 2` then a newline and
    the one non-matched object's diff lines `  {label}: {path}: expected {v}, got {v2}`

Scenario: at_most and none report the offenders, not the misses
  Given two of three selected matching @value with `matcher: at_most: 1` (or `none`)
  Then message ends `... expected at most 1` / `... expected none` followed by the two
    matched objects as `  {label} (matched)` lines, while the value-lane all/any/exact/
    at_least failure detail instead lists non-matched objects with their JSON diffs

Scenario: count-lane bare matchers
  Given selector selecting three objects, asserts with no `value` key
  Then `all`, `any`, `at_least: 2`, `at_most: 3` pass printing `3 match`;
    `exact: 2` fails `3 match, expected exactly 2`; `none` fails `3 match, expected none`
  And at zero selected `all`/`any` fail `0 match, expected at least one` (the hint fast
    path exempts only `none`/`at_most`, so a bare `all` still gets the hint message, not
    this fail phrase)

Scenario: appslug branches
  Given @appslug with @pkg and @inst both the same long instance name (over 28 chars)
  Then the name returns whole — the `pkg == inst` shortcut ignores the 28 budget
  Given @inst `someinstance` and @pkg `longpackageoverthelimit`
  Then the composite `{inst}-{pkg}` comes back cut to exactly 28 Unicode scalars

Example:
  full at_least fail message: `1/3 match, expected at least 2` + newline +
    `  Deployment/prod/api: .spec.replicas: expected 3, got 1, .spec.template: expected {...}, got <missing>` +
    newline + `  ConfigMap/api-cfg: [0]: no match found for {...}`
